  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Design Framework**\n\nI\'m focusing on incorporating custom CSS variables and utility classes into `src/index.css`. This is critical for ensuring consistent styling across the interface. My aim is to achieve smooth transitions, standardized font treatments, and custom scrollbars, while also applying tabular numbers and implementing a modular design system.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve been working on defining crucial data structures in `/src/types.ts`. I\'m creating types for `BudgetItem`, `Transaction`, `TabType`, `FilterOptions`, and `NotificationItem`. I\'m ensuring everything aligns well. In `/src/data/initialData.ts`, I\'m populating realistic, pre-populated data that matches the exact screenshots, covering budget categories like Dining Out, Housing, and Shopping, along with other categories.\n\n\n**Refining Financial Calculations**\n\nI\'m focused on developing robust financial formatting and calculation utilities within `/src/utils/formatters.ts`. I\'m prioritizing safe currency formatting, percentage calculation with error handling, and implementing over-budget calculations that gracefully manage edge cases like zero division and negative limits, displaying clear, visual feedback.\n\\n\\n\nI\'m also working on constructing a rich initial transaction log that will populate the History tab and Analysis charts.\nFinally, I\'m constructing the `/src/components/Navigation.tsx` module, and fleshing out the responsive sidebar, mobile header and mobile bottom navigation components.\n\n\n**Constructing User Interface**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `/src/components/Navigation.tsx` module, and finalizing the responsive sidebar, mobile header, and mobile bottom navigation components. I\'m also adding smooth animations. The desktop header, including section title, notification popover, and profile drawer, is coming together. I\'ve begun working on `/src/components/HomeTab.tsx`, aiming for a quick overview of financial health, recent activity, and smart insights. I\'m starting work on `/src/components/BudgetTab.tsx`, paying attention to the precise screenshot layout, including Bento Summary Grid, Active Budgets section, and over-budget handling.\n\n\n**Developing Tabbed Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of several tabs. In `/src/components/HistoryTab.tsx`, I\'m implementing a detailed transaction ledger. It includes search, filtering by category and type, sorting, and a date range picker, as well as CSV/JSON export and handling for empty search results. `/src/components/AnalysisTab.tsx` is where I\'m working with Recharts for visual charts, including expense breakdowns, budget comparisons, and spending trends, plus a financial health score. Finally, in `/src/components/Modals`, I\'m constructing `AddTransactionModal.tsx` for logging expenses and income with real-time budget updates and warnings.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 910825926
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
